[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4581864652","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119876#issuecomment-4581864652","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119876","id":4581864652,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABERm0zA","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-30T05:45:16Z","updated_at":"2026-05-30T05:45:16Z","body":"Given that `clear` is exposed, wouldn't adjusting `clear` to gracefully handle autoloads make more sense?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4581864652/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4582548931","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119876#issuecomment-4582548931","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119876","id":4582548931,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABESQlww","user":{"login":"Lefrec","id":158512522,"node_id":"U_kgDOCXK1ig","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/158512522?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lefrec","html_url":"https://github.com/Lefrec","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lefrec/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lefrec/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lefrec/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lefrec/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lefrec/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lefrec/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lefrec/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lefrec/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lefrec/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-30T10:33:58Z","updated_at":"2026-05-30T10:33:58Z","body":"I can try that,  we would change `autoload_remove` to use this adjusted `clear` as well right ?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4582548931/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4582968781","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119876#issuecomment-4582968781","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119876","id":4582968781,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABESqNzQ","user":{"login":"Lefrec","id":158512522,"node_id":"U_kgDOCXK1ig","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/158512522?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lefrec","html_url":"https://github.com/Lefrec","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lefrec/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lefrec/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lefrec/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lefrec/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lefrec/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lefrec/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lefrec/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lefrec/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lefrec/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-30T13:33:11Z","updated_at":"2026-05-30T13:33:11Z","body":"I just noticed that the section in `_autoload_button_pressed` removing autoloads when pressing the trashcan button in project settings doesn't use `clear` either and set to null value like in `autoload_remove`. \r\nSame thing in `autoload_add` for the undo action : \r\n```cpp\r\nif (ProjectSettings::get_singleton()->has_setting(name)) {\r\n\tundo_redo->add_undo_property(ProjectSettings::get_singleton(), name, GLOBAL_GET(name));\r\n} else {\r\n\tundo_redo->add_undo_property(ProjectSettings::get_singleton(), name, Variant());\r\n}\r\n```\r\n`clear` is only used when renaming, while setting to null value is commonly used since `_set` already has a logic for removing the null autoloads : \r\n```cpp\r\nif (p_value.get_type() == Variant::NIL) {\r\n\tprops.erase(p_name);\r\n\tif (p_name.operator String().begins_with(\"autoload/\")) {\r\n\t\tString node_name = p_name.operator String().get_slicec('/', 1);\r\n\t\tif (autoloads.has(node_name)) {\r\n\t\t\tremove_autoload(node_name);\r\n\t\t}\r\n```\r\n\r\n`_set` also handles removing global_groups the same way, if we changed `clear` to handle removing autoloads it should probably handle removing global_groups as well, which would be redundant with what is already in `_set`.\r\n\r\nSo I think setting to null value like I proposed is the right way considering the existing code. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4582968781/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4745754175","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119876#issuecomment-4745754175","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119876","id":4745754175,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABGt52Pw","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-18T20:11:05Z","updated_at":"2026-06-23T19:21:34Z","body":"Could you squash your commits? See our [pull request guidelines](https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/organization/pull_requests/creating_pull_requests.html#the-interactive-rebase) for more information","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comme